{
  "_readme": [
    "Single source of truth for every property transaction rate the site quotes.",
    "js/costs.js renders whatever is in here — no rate is written into the code.",
    "",
    "IMPORTANT: while \"verified\" is false the calculator says so on the page, in",
    "amber, and refuses to present itself as authoritative. Set it true, with your",
    "name and the date, once you have checked each line — and only then.",
    "",
    "scripts/tax-watch.mjs re-reads every source below on a schedule and checks",
    "whether the figure we show still appears next to the words that identify it",
    "on the live page. Confirmed rates get a lastSeen date. Ones that no longer",
    "match are reported, and where the page is unambiguous the new value lands in",
    "\"proposed\" and opens a pull request. Nothing is ever applied automatically:",
    "these numbers sit in front of buyers working out what they can afford."
  ],
